---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description="How this site & my practices have been made"
>
  <div class="one-column">
    <div class="headerContainer textContent colophon">
      <header class="colophon-intro">
        <h1 class="uniform">(colophon)</h1>
        <p class="colophon-lede">
          <i>how this site & my practices have been made.</i>
        </p>
        <p>
          This site is a home I keep tending rather than a portfolio I finish.
          It's hand-built, open source, and a little bit alive: you're rarely
          the only one here.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="colophon-section">
        <h2>Site</h2>
        <dl class="colophon-list">
          <dt>framework</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, with
            <a href="https://react.dev/">React</a> islands for the interactive
            bits and view transitions so the sidebar and footer persist between
            pages.
          </dd>

          <dt>multiplayer</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="/creation/playhtml">playhtml</a>, my open-source library
            for shared, real-time web elements. It powers the live cursors, the
            guestbook, reactions, and the objects you can move around.
            <a href="https://github.com/nanostores/nanostores">Nanostores</a>
            keep things like chat around as you navigate.
          </dd>

          <dt>styles</dt>
          <dd>
            Hand-written SCSS on a small set of shared tokens (one type scale,
            one spacing scale), plus a bit of Tailwind.
          </dd>

          <dt>content</dt>
          <dd>
            Creations and newsletter issues live in a
            <a href="https://coda.io/">Coda</a> doc and get imported at build
            time. Posts are MDX. The status line pulls from
            <a href="/creation/statusspencerchangme">my status feed</a>, which
            checks the platforms I use every hour.
          </dd>

          <dt>hosting</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a> Pages and
            Workers, built with <a href="https://bun.sh/">Bun</a>.
          </dd>

          <dt>source</dt>
          <dd>
            Open on <a href="https://github.com/spencerc99/home">GitHub</a>.
            Feel free to borrow anything you like.
          </dd>

          <dt>feeds</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>, or
            <a href="https://spencerchang.substack.com">the newsletter</a> if
            you prefer email.
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="colophon-section">
        <h2>Type & texture</h2>
        <dl class="colophon-list">
          <dt>body</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="https://ohnotype.co/fonts/vulf-sans">Vulf Sans</a> by Oh
            No Type Co., for everything you read.
          </dd>

          <dt>labels</dt>
          <dd>
            <span class="colophon-mono">Sono</span>, a monospace by Tyler Finck
            (<a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Sono">Google Fonts</a>),
            for page titles, dates, and these little labels.
          </dd>

          <dt>background</dt>
          <dd>
            A photo of sunlight seeping through my jacket lining on a sunny day
            in Alamo Square.
          </dd>

          <dt>nav</dt>
          <dd>Emoji, because every page deserves a little mascot.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="colophon-section">
        <h2>Little details</h2>
        <ul class="colophon-details">
          <li>
            Other visitors show up as cursors. Each page has its own room, so
            you'll only see people reading the same thing you are.
          </li>
          <li>
            The <a href="/about">about page</a> has a guestbook. I read every
            letter.
          </li>
          <li>
            The footer holds trinkets: the last vignette I took and
            <a href="/friends">my friends webring</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Every outbound link carries
            <span class="colophon-mono">utm_source=invited_by_Spencer_Chang</span
            >, so the other side knows who sent you.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="colophon-section">
        <h2>Inspirations</h2>
        <ul class="colophon-details">
          <li>
            Thank you to <a href="https://robinsloan.com/">Robin Sloan</a> for
            the "invited_by" UTM idea, which I borrowed directly from him.
          </li>
          <li>
            Thank you to the personal websites of
            <a href="/friends">my friends</a>, which make me want to keep this
            one weird.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="colophon-section">
        <h2>People</h2>
        <p class="colophon-note">
          A non-exhaustive, sporadically updated list of people (and
          collectives) who have inspired me.
        </p>
        <ul class="colophon-people">
          <li>Sarah Sze</li>
          <li>Nam June Paik</li>
          <li>Yoko Ono & Fluxus</li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://lauren-mccarthy.com/">Lauren Lee McCarthy</a>
          </li>
          <li>Olafur Eliasson</li>
          <li>Lee Mingwei</li>
          <li>Isamu Noguchi</li>
          <li>Oki Sato</li>
          <li><a href="https://worrydream.com/">Bret Victor</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://mschf.com/">MSCHF</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://wiki.xxiivv.com/site/merveilles.html">Merveilles</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://panic.com/">Panic</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .colophon {
    max-width: var(--sp-measure);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-space-16);
  }

  .colophon p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .colophon-intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-space-3);
  }

  .colophon-intro h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .colophon-lede {
    font-size: var(--sp-text-lg);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .colophon-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-space-4);
  }

  .colophon-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sp-text-xl);
    line-height: 1.3;
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--sp-color-accent);
  }

  /* Label / value rows: Sono label on the left, Vulf text on the right. */
  .colophon-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--sp-space-4) var(--sp-space-6);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .colophon-list dt {
    font-family: var(--sp-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sp-text-sm);
    line-height: var(--sp-leading-body);
    color: var(--sp-color-text-subtle);
    /* Nudge the smaller label onto the first line's baseline. */
    padding-top: 0.1em;
  }

  .colophon-list dd {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--sp-leading-body);
  }

  .colophon-details {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--sp-space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-space-3);
    line-height: var(--sp-leading-body);
  }

  .colophon-details li {
    margin: 0;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .colophon-details li::marker {
    color: var(--sp-color-accent);
  }

  .colophon-note {
    color: var(--sp-color-text-subtle);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .colophon-people {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(11rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-space-2) var(--sp-space-6);
  }

  .colophon-people li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .colophon-mono {
    font-family: var(--sp-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .colophon {
      gap: var(--sp-space-8);
    }

    .colophon-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .colophon-list dt {
      padding-top: 0;
    }

    .colophon-list dd + dt {
      margin-top: var(--sp-space-4);
    }
  }
</style>
